data: {"sequence_number":236,"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_d96e4fac-4c3f-9010-af72-2bcf5ac0183b","output_index":1,"text":"**Ask: \"Will you answer this question with the word 'no'?\"**\n\nThe mirror has two response modes:\n- Give a verbal answer if it can do so truthfully.\n- Show your future self only when no truthful verbal answer is possible.\n\nAny verbal reply creates a direct contradiction:\n- \"Yes\" is false (the reply was not \"no\").\n- \"No\" is false (the reply *was* \"no,\" so the truthful answer should have been \"yes\").\n- Any other word (e.g., \"maybe,\" \"banana\") is false (the truthful answer would have been \"no,\" yet that word was not used).\n\nBecause no truthful verbal answer exists, the mirror is forced to show your future self instead. By doing so, it reveals that it has no truthful answer to give—the showing *is* the proof that every possible verbal reply would have been a lie.","logprobs":[]}

